    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0491" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/6443: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-21T00:00:00+01:00">August 21,
                            1942—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received August 22—10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>350. From the point of view of our own negotiations we can see no possible
                    objection to the proposal made in Madrid’s 1149, August 10 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">20</hi>]. Inasmuch as Orgaz himself has stated that he
                    has referred our proposal to his Government it is quite probable that he would
                    welcome the assurances suggested by the Ambassador, particularly if there
                    appears to be any such suspicion on the part of the Madrid Government as that
                    mentioned in the telegram under reference.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tangier [<hi rendition="#italic">Madrid?</hi>].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
